<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2015/06/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>blip</id>
    <version>1.0.0</version>
    <title>Blip: Send Files in a Click</title>
    <authors>Blip Studio Inc.</authors>
    <owners>paradonym</owners>
    <projectUrl>https://blip.net/</projectUrl>
    <licenseUrl>https://blip.net/terms-of-service</licenseUrl>
    <packageSourceUrl>https://github.com/paradonym/blip-chocolatey</PackageSourceUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <iconUrl>https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/paradonym/blip-chocolatey@main/icons/blip.svg</iconUrl>
    <copyright>2026 Blip Studio Inc.</copyright>
    <summary>Send files and folders of any size directly to other devices and people, fast and end-to-end encrypted.</summary>
    <description>
Blip is a cross-platform app for sending files and folders of any size directly to your other devices or to other people, without uploading them to a cloud service first. Transfers are end-to-end encrypted and resume after network interruptions.

This package installs Blip (Microsoft Store product ID `9N7JSXC1SJK6`) using `winget` from the `msstore` source. The package does not contain the app itself, and updates are managed by the Microsoft Store.

## Requirements

* Windows 10 version 1809 (build 17763) or later, or Windows 11
* `winget` (App Installer), provided via the `winget` package dependency
* Access to the Microsoft Store (the install runs in the context of a signed-in user, not as SYSTEM)

## Notes

* Blip is proprietary software. It is free for non-commercial use; commercial use requires a paid plan (see https://blip.net/pricing).
* If Blip is already installed, the package install completes without changes. Uninstalling the package also removes the app.
    </description>
    <releaseNotes>Initial version of the package. Installs the current Microsoft Store version of Blip via winget.</releaseNotes>
    <tags>blip file-transfer file-sharing freeware winget msstore</tags>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency id="winget" />
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
